Spec: Spec Kit SpecDD Integration Lab

Platform: Spec Kit/SpecDD/Node.js/Python/Shell

Purpose:
  Integrate the Spec Kit change lifecycle with SpecDD persistent system contracts through a thin derived bridge while preserving each system as the authority for its own model.

Structure:
  ./integration: Bridge extension and preset source governed by local specs
  ./fixtures: Integration-test systems governed by local specs
  ./docs: Project design and development documentation
  ./scripts: Bootstrap and repository maintenance automation

Owns:
  ./docs/spec.md
  ./docs/TODO.md
  ./docs/development.md
  ./scripts/bootstrap.sh
  ./dev-scripts.include
  ./HUMAN-REQUEST.md
  ./DEBUGGING.md

References:
  ./docs/spec.md
  ./docs/development.md

Must:
  Spec Kit remains the canonical change lifecycle and feature-task system.
  SpecDD remains the canonical persistent system specification and authority model.
  Bridge mechanics delegate SpecDD resolution to the installed SpecDD tooling rather than independently interpreting SpecDD semantics.
  Derived integration state remains reconstructible from authoritative Spec Kit artifacts and SpecDD specifications.
  Bridge source remains separate from generated Spec Kit state.
  Authority changes take effect for implementation only after the changed SpecDD state is resolved in a new authority context.

Must not:
  Patch or fork upstream Spec Kit or SpecDD core to provide bridge behavior.
  Maintain a copied SpecDD constraint set in Spec Kit feature artifacts or derived bridge state.
  Synchronize Spec Kit feature tasks with SpecDD `Tasks` entries.
  Automatically edit `.sdd` files or relax SpecDD authority as bridge behavior.
